%% title: The steps of an ACR, a survey and an incident
%% desc: An ACR is started, scored, completed, and can be reopened. A survey goes from draft to open to closed, and results show after it closes. An incident is reported and can be withdrawn with a reason.
flowchart LR
  subgraph ACR["ACR"]
    A1["Start"]:::admin --> A2["Score<br/>saves itself"]:::teacher --> A3["Completed"]:::guardian
    A3 -->|"Reopen"| A2
  end
  subgraph SV["Survey"]
    S1["Draft"]:::note --> S2["Open"]:::teacher --> S3["Closed"]:::note --> S4["Results show"]:::guardian
  end
  subgraph IN["Incident"]
    I1["Report"]:::admin --> I2["In the list"]:::note
    I2 -->|"Withdraw"| I3["Leaves the list"]:::note
  end
  classDef teacher fill:#e7f5ff,stroke:#1c7ed6,color:#0b3d66
  classDef admin fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7a2e05
  classDef guardian fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
  classDef note fill:#f1f3f5,stroke:#868e96,color:#343a40
